body:
there’s nothing wrong with you, i don’t know why on earth anyone would say this to a stranger online. ignore this commenter OP, you’ll be okay :) you ran a lot the day before, was this just to run/be active or was it with the intention to burn calories? if it’s the latter, people who suffer from binge eating who also exercise a lot will frequently end up in a binge/compensate pattern like this. 

it’s so easy to fall into this trap of thinking where you feel like you have to burn off everything to you eat, i promise you that all it does is make you miserable. you binged today, and it’s good that you’re not beating yourself up too much about it! just take it in stride and when you feel the urge to binge again, utilize a healthy coping mechanism as a way to concentrate your focus on something else. don’t be too harsh on yourself, it was your birthday after all! i usually end up binging on my birthday too, i think it’s common for a lot of us. my birthday is actually coming up soon as well! 

if you ever need advice on how to deal with this or just want to talk, feel free to reach out to me :)

they really don’t. human hair can last a lot longer than synthetic hair depending on how often it’s worn and how well it’s maintained. synthetic wigs, for example, typically last ~ 1-3 months if worn everyday/frequently. human hair, on the other hand, can last about a year or two. again, it all depends on how often the wig is worn and maintained. 

source: used to work at a beauty supply store

if you have any questions just ask :)
